message.content:
Sure! Below is a minimal example of an **interactive card** that rotates (spins) when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML + CSS** – no JavaScript needed.

---

## 1️⃣ Markup (HTML)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-front">
      <h2>Front Side</h2>
      <p>This is the front of the card.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-back">
      <h2>Back Side</h2>
      <p>Hover again to see the back!</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

* `card-wrapper` keeps the card centered and provides perspective.  
* Inside we have two faces: `.card-front` and `.card-back`.

---

## 2️⃣ Styling (CSS)

Create a file called `styles.css` (or put the `<style>` block inside the `<head>`).

```css
/* ---------- Global ---------- */
body {
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  background: #f0f0f0;
  display:flex;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  height:100vh;
  margin:0;
}

/* ---------- Wrapper ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- Card ---------- */
.card {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
  transition: transform 0.8s ease; /* Smooth rotation */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect: rotate 180° around Y-axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* ---------- Faces ---------- */
.card > div {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide backside when flipped */
  border-radius: 10px;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  padding:20px;
  box-sizing:border-box;
}

.card-front {
  background:#fff;
  color:#333;
}

.card-back {
  background:#333;
  color:#fff;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Position back face behind front */
}
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| 1 | The `.card-wrapper` gives the container a *perspective* so that 3D transforms look realistic. |
| 2 | The `.card` element has `transform-style: preserve-3d` so its children keep their 3D positions. |
| 3 | Each face (`.card-front`, `.card-back`) is absolutely positioned on top of each other. |
| 4 | `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that is turned away from the viewer. |
| 5 | On hover, the `.card` rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back face. |

---

## 🎨 Customization Ideas

| Property | What to change | Example |
|----------|----------------|---------|
| `width / height` | Size of the card | `width: 350px; height: 250px;` |
| `background` | Color or image | `background: url('image.jpg') center/cover;` |
| `transition` | Speed & easing | `transition: transform 1s cubic-bezier(.68,-0.55,.27,1.55);` |
| `rotateY(180deg)` | Flip direction | `rotateX(180deg)` flips vertically instead of horizontally. |

Feel free to copy the code into your project and tweak it as you like! If you need more advanced effects (e.g., adding shadows, gradients, or 3D depth), just let me know.
